{
  "_how_to_rebalance": [
    "Which Api test classes each CI shard runs. Read by .github/scripts/shard-args.py; the shards are the matrix entries api-1 to api-4 of the `tests` job in .github/workflows/ci.yml.",
    "Each class is written Namespace.Class, exactly as xUnit names it (no wildcards), and may be listed for one shard only. A class listed nowhere runs in the shard named by \"remainder\", so a new test class is never skipped; it just is not balanced until someone lists it here.",
    "Shards were balanced on 2026-10-06 from the run of that day (about 16900 test seconds over 2195 tests; the nine classes with the most test time at their measured seconds, every other class at about 7.2 seconds a test, capped at 240 s a class). Estimated test seconds then: api-1 about 4390 (561 tests, 48 classes), api-2 about 4390 (553, 47), api-3 about 4390 (545, 48), api-4 (the remainder, kept lighter on purpose so new classes do not tip it over) about 3720 (537, 46).",
    "To rebalance: open a CI run's summary page. Each `tests (api-N)` job has a Test suites table (its Minutes and Tests) and a Slowest tests section (the Test seconds of its suite and its 15 classes with the most test time). Move a class from the slowest shard to the fastest by deleting its line from one list and adding it to another. To move a class into the remainder shard, only delete it from its list; to move one out of the remainder shard, only add it to another list. Keep the remainder shard the lightest.",
    "Check a change without running a test: python3 .github/scripts/shard-args.py api-2 /tmp/api-2.rsp /tmp/api-2.xml 120 (it warns about a name that is not a test class any more and fails on a class listed twice or a misspelt name)."
  ],
